# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env itself
# (it's already in .gitignore) — this file exists only to document what's
# needed to run the app, with no real secrets in it.
#
# VITE_ prefixed vars are exposed to client-side code (Vite convention) —
# anything without that prefix is server-only and must NEVER be given a
# VITE_ prefix, or it would ship straight into the browser bundle.

# Supabase project URL and public anon key — from your Supabase project's
# Settings > API page. Safe to expose to the client; every real access
# control is enforced by this project's RLS policies (see
# supabase/migrations/*.sql), not by keeping this key secret.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Supabase service-role key — from the same Settings > API page. Bypasses
# all Row Level Security. Must only ever be read in server-side code
# (src/lib/moodle-server.ts, src/lib/admin-server.ts,
# src/lib/moodle-cron-handler.ts) — never imported into anything that ends
# up in the browser bundle. Treat this like a root database password.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Shared secret the /api/moodle/cron-sync endpoint requires on the
# x-cron-secret header — anyone without it gets a 401. This same value
# must also be set wherever the real Supabase pg_cron job is configured
# (see supabase/migrations/0018_moodle_sync_cron.sql's own comment).
# Generate a long random string; regenerate it if it's ever exposed.
MOODLE_CRON_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string

# Not read by the app itself — nothing in src/ consumes this. Handy only
# for manually testing the Gemini API directly (e.g. via curl) during
# development; safe to leave unset.
# TEST_GEMINI_KEY=your-own-gemini-api-key-for-manual-testing

# Google OAuth (sign-in with Google) is NOT configured via env vars at
# all — no code in this repo reads a GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET. Sign-in goes
# through Supabase Auth (supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth,
# src/routes/login.tsx), so the Google Client ID + Client Secret must be
# pasted into the Supabase Dashboard instead: Authentication > Sign In /
# Providers > Google.
